; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10283  
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10284  /* Justification for module-specific MISRA deviations:
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10285  
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10286  MD_CanIf_Rule8.3:
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10287    Reason: For parameter DataPtr the typedef Can_<Infix>_PduInfoPtrType with a possible infix is not used to be compatible 
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10288            with inxfixed and not infixed CAN drivers.
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10289    Risk: Different datatypes for parameter DataPtr in definition and declaration.
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10290    Prevention: Code inspection.
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10291  
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10292  MD_CanIf_Rule8.9:
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10293    Reason: Constant tables are kept at a central location for a better overview and maintenance.
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10294    Risk: Name conflict.
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10295    Prevention: Compiler optimize and check for name conflicts.
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10296  
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10297  MD_CanIf_Rule10.5_4342:
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10298    Reason: The different mode types are abstracted with the enum CanIf_PduGetModeType/ CanIf_PduSetModeType.
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10299            But a lookup table CanIfState from a basic unsigned data type is used to get a requested mode.
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10300            This leads to a runtime efficient code.
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10301    Risk: Inconsistency between mode types in CanIf_PduGetModeType/ CanIf_PduSetModeType enum and CanIfState lookup table.
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10302    Prevention: Code inspection and test of the different configurations in the component test.
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10303  
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10304  MD_CanIf_CastUintToEnum:
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10305    Reason: Element of enum CanIf_ControllerModeType is determinded from look up table CanIf_CanCtrlState2CanIfCtrlModeLookUp[],
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10306            which contains the enum elements as unsigned integer values.
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10307    Risk: Inconsistency between elements from CanIf_ControllerModeType enum and unsigned integer values in lookup table
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10308          CanIf_CanCtrlState2CanIfCtrlModeLookUp[].
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10309    Prevention: Code inspection and test of the different configurations in the component test.
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10310  
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10311  MD_CanIf_CastEnumToDiffEnum:
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10312    Reason: Ensures same behaviour in function for both enums CanIf_ControllerModeType and Can_ControllerStateType, if passed
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10313            controller mode is not valid. Both enums have the same valid value range.
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10314    Risk: None.
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10315    Prevention: Code inspection and test of the different configurations in the component test.
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10316  
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10317  MD_CanIf_Rule11.1:
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10318    Reason: Cast to different pointer type required to avoid compiler warning due to usage of a union of function pointer types.
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10319    Risk: None due to fact that function pointer are used.
