; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10740  /**********************************************************************************************************************
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10741   *  FETA JUSTIFICATIONS
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10742   *********************************************************************************************************************/
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10743  
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10744  /* FETA_JUSTIFICATION_BEGIN
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10745  
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10746  \ID FETA_CANIF_1
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10747  \DESCRIPTION The for loop iterates over all configured Tx-Buffers, which are assigned to a CAN controller.
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10748               The number of iteration is limited and statically given by the number of configured Tx-Buffers
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10749               at a CAN controller.
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10750  
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10751  \COUNTERMEASURE \N The number of iteration is therefore not influencend by the processing process (push, pop and cancel Tx-PDUs)
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10752                     of the Tx-Buffers.
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10753  
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10754  \ID FETA_CANIF_2
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10755  \DESCRIPTION The while loop iterates over the currently queued Tx-PDUs in the Tx-Buffer to clear their cancel settings.
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10756               The number of iteration depends on the currently number of queued Tx-PDUs in the Tx-Buffer.
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10757  
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10758  \COUNTERMEASURE \N The while loop is locked by CANIF_EXCLUSIVE_AREA_1 to prevent push, pop and cancel Tx-PDUs while processing the
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10759                     Tx-Buffer. This ensures a termination of the loop.
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10760  
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10761  \ID FETA_CANIF_3
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10762  \DESCRIPTION The while loop has complex termination conditions.
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10763  \COUNTERMEASURE \D CanIf_RxIndicationSubLinearSearch
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10764  
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10765  \ID FETA_CANIF_4
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10766  \DESCRIPTION The while loop has external termination condition computation (calls to CanIf_RxIndicationSubReceptionPduMode).
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10767  \COUNTERMEASURE \D DSGN-CanIfDiag2274
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10768  
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10769  \ID FETA_CANIF_5
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10770  \DESCRIPTION The while loop iterates over the currently queued Tx-PDUs in the Tx-Buffer to find the next not canceled Tx-PDU.
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10771               The number of iteration depends on the currently number of the queued Tx-PDUs in the Tx-Buffer.
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10772  
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10773  \COUNTERMEASURE \N The while loop is locked by CANIF_EXCLUSIVE_AREA_2 to prevent push, pop and cancel Tx-PDUs while processing the
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10774                     Tx-Buffer. This ensures a termination of the loop.
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10775  
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10776  \ID FETA_CANIF_6
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10777  \DESCRIPTION The for loop iterates over all configured queue flags (each flag repesent one Tx-PDU that can be queued) of the
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10778               Tx-Buffer to clear them.
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10779               The number of iteration is limited and statically given by the number of configured queue flags of the Tx-Buffer.
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10780  \COUNTERMEASURE \N The number of iteration is therefore not influencend by the processing process (push, pop and cancel Tx-PDUs)
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10781                     of the Tx-Buffer.
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10782  
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10783  \ID FETA_CANIF_7
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10784  \DESCRIPTION The while loop termination is determined by values from the following calculations
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10785               startPos = (uint8)((PduInfoPtr->SduLength) - 1u)
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10786               endPos = (uint8)(endPos - CANIF_CFG_TX_TXMETADATALENGTH(localPduPtr->swPduHandle))
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10787  \COUNTERMEASURE \N The variable PduInfoPtr->SduLength (value 0 - 64) is checked (>=) against CANIF_CFG_TX_TXMETADATALENGTH(localPduPtr->swPduHandle) (value 1 -4).
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10788                     Therefore the value for PduInfoPtr->SduLength is ensured to be between 1 and 64. The value for startPos is between 0 and 63 after the calaculation.
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10789                     The variable endPos is first set to PduInfoPtr->SduLength (value 1 - 64, regarding to check above).
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10790                     The value for endPos is between 0 and 60 after the calaculation.
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10791                     Therefore the for loop terminates always after between 0 and 3 iterations.
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10792  
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10793  \ID FETA_CANIF_8
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10794  \DESCRIPTION The for loop termination is determined by a value returned by an parameterized GenData access.
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10795  \COUNTERMEASURE \N The argument for the parameterized GenData access is checked by the caller for a valid access to the table CanIf_RxPduConfig[].
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10796                     Therefore it is a strictly monotonic for loop.
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10797  
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10798  \ID FETA_CANIF_9
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10799  \DESCRIPTION The for loop iterates over the currently queued Tx-PDUs in the Tx-Buffer to find the Tx-PDU with the highest priority.
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10800               The number of iteration depends on the number and the priority of the currently queued Tx-PDUs in the Tx-Buffer.
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10801  \COUNTERMEASURE \N The for loop is locked by CANIF_EXCLUSIVE_AREA_2 to prevent push, pop and cancel Tx-PDUs while processing the
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10802                     Tx-Buffer. This ensures a termination of the loop.
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10803  
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10804  \ID FETA_CANIF_10
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10805  \DESCRIPTION The for loop termination is determined by a value from the calculation dlc_checksum - 1u.
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10806  \COUNTERMEASURE \N The variable dlc_checksum is checked against zero and CANIF_CFG_MAXTXDLC_PLUS_DATACHECKSUM (maximum value 64).
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10807                     Therefore the for loop terminates always after between 1 and 63 iterations.
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10808  
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10809  \ID FETA_CANIF_11
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10810  \DESCRIPTION The for loop termination is determined by a value from the calculation CanDlc - 1u.
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10811  \COUNTERMEASURE \N The variable CanDlc is checked against zero and in the caller function against 8/64.
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10812                     Therefore the for loop terminates always after between 1 and 63 iterations.
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10813  
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10814  \ID FETA_CANIF_12
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10815  \DESCRIPTION The for loop iterates over all configured queue states (each state repesent one Tx-PDU that can be queued) of the
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10816               Tx-Buffer to clear them.
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10817               The number of iteration is limited and statically given by the number of configured queue states of the Tx-Buffer.
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10818  \COUNTERMEASURE \N The number of iteration is therefore not influencend by the processing process (push, pop and cancel Tx-PDUs)
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10819                     of the Tx-Buffer.
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10820  
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10821  \ID FETA_CANIF_13
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10822  \DESCRIPTION The for loop iterates over the currently queued Tx-PDUs in the Tx-Buffer to find the Tx-PDU with the highest priority.
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10823               The number of iteration depends on the number and the priority of the currently queued Tx-PDUs in the Tx-Buffer.
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10824  \COUNTERMEASURE \N The for loop is locked by CANIF_EXCLUSIVE_AREA_2 to prevent push, pop and cancel Tx-PDUs while processing the
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10825                     Tx-Buffer. This ensures a termination of the loop.
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10826  
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10827  \ID FETA_CANIF_14
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10828  \DESCRIPTION The while loop has complex termination conditions.
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10829  \COUNTERMEASURE \D CanIf_RxIndicationSubBinarySearch
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10830  
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10831  \ID FETA_CANIF_X
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10832  \DESCRIPTION The for loop termination is determined by a value returned by an static GenData access.
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10833  \COUNTERMEASURE \N The GenData are accessed via the CanIf_ConfigDataPtr. The CanIf_ConfigDataPtr is set and cheked in CanIf_Init().
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10834                     This ensures a valid GenData access and a termination of the loop (strictly monotonic for loop).
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10835  
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10836  \ID FETA_CANIF_Y
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10837  \DESCRIPTION The for loop termination is determined by a value from the calculation
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10838               CANIF_J1939_CTRL_ADDR_TBL_SIZE - 1u .
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10839  \COUNTERMEASURE \N CANIF_J1939_CTRL_ADDR_TBL_SIZE is statically defined to 256 in CanIf.c.
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10840                     Therefore the for loop terminates always after 255 iterations (strictly monotonic for loop).
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10841  
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10842  \ID FETA_CANIF_Z
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10843  \DESCRIPTION The for loop termination is determined by a value from the calculation
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10844               sizeof(CanIf_CtrlStates) / sizeof(CanIf_CtrlStatesType) .
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10845  \COUNTERMEASURE \N The number of iteration is limited by sizeof of corresponding type and corresponding variable
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10846                     (strictly monotonic for loop).
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10847  
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10848  FETA_JUSTIFICATION_END */
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10849  
; ..\BSW364\CanIf\Implementation\CanIf.c	 10850  /**********************************************************************************************************************
